# Design Guide

## Vision
The app should feel like a premium, calm, modern AI workspace: a little like Notion + ChatGPT + local desktop app. The user should feel trust, clarity, and speed.

## Core UX Principles

### 1. Less is more
- Never overload the screen with controls
- Keep every page focused on one task
- Use whitespace intentionally
- Hide advanced controls behind a compact Settings drawer

### 2. The page should feel like a book, not a dashboard
- Left sidebar = book/library/collections
- Center = main reading/writing surface
- Right sidebar = optional context or reasoning
- Use a strong typography system instead of colorful clutter

### 3. Trust and clarity
- Show reasoning only when the user asks for it
- Let the user toggle visibility of reasoning and memory
- Label things clearly: `Reasoning`, `Final Answer`, `Memory`, `Context`

## Recommended Layout

### Main App Shell
```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Header: Title | Search | Model Status | Settings                     │
├───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Sidebar               │ Main content area                             │
│ - Conversations       │ - Current chat                                 │
│ - Folders             │ - Message stream                              │
│ - Quick prompts       │ - Reasoning panel (optional)                  │
│ - Settings shortcuts  │ - Input composer                              │
├───────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Footer: Local status | memory usage | model health | connection state │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Visual Style

### Color system
- Background: warm white / soft gray (#F7F5F2)
- Card: white (#FFFFFF)
- Border: subtle gray (#E8E3DE)
- Primary: deep slate/ink (#1F2937)
- Accent: muted blue (#496BFF) or muted sage (#3C6E71)
- Warning: amber (#D97706)
- Success: green (#1F8A70)

### Typography
- Use `Inter`, `Segoe UI`, or `SF Pro Display`
- Headings: medium weight, strong spacing
- Body: comfortable readability
- Use clean sentence case

### Motion
- Use subtle animation only
- 150-220ms transitions
- Smooth panel slide-ins
- Avoid flashy or noisy effects

## UI Patterns

### 1. Chat bubble system
- User messages: soft slate or blue fill, subtle shadow
- AI messages: white cards with thin border
- Reasoning messages: muted amber or gray panels

### 2. Compact controls
- Keep controls near the composer
- Use icon buttons with labels only when necessary
- Model selection in a compact dropdown

### 3. Memory panel
- Show `Relevant memories`, `Recent context`, `Known facts`
- Keep it visible but secondary

### 4. Empty state
- When no conversation exists, show:
  - `New conversation`
  - 4 quick prompts
  - `Local-only private mode`

## Modern App Features That Matter
- Dark mode toggle
- Compact mode / focus mode
- Real-time memory insights
- Reasoning panel toggle
- Streamed response animation
- Smooth conversation switching
- Private local mode indicator

## Recommended Page Flow

### Page 1: Start screen
- App title
- Small welcome text
- Quick prompt chips
- Recent conversations

### Page 2: Main workspace
- Chat area center
- Sidebar conversations
- Optional reasoning pane

### Page 3: Settings drawer
- Model config
- Memory settings
- Local database status
- Export/import conversations

## Final Rule
If the UI looks too busy, remove something. The app should feel calm, private, and premium.
